{"name":"Porch Song","hex":"#566f8c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered entrance to a building, whether taken from the interior, and forming a sort of vestibule within the main wall, or projecting without and with a separate roof. A porch often has chair(s), table(s) and swings.","A portico; a covered walk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch"},{"term":"song","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical composition with lyrics for voice or voices, performed by singing.","Any musical composition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch","wikidata":"Q816741"},{"title":"Song","blocks":[{"text":"A song is a musical composition performed by the human voice. The voice often carries the melody using patterns of sound and silence. Songs have a structure, such as the common ABA form, and are usually made of sections that are repeated or performed with variation later. A song without instruments is said to be a cappella."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg/330px-Billie_Holiday%2C_Downbeat%2C_New_York%2C_N.Y.%2C_ca._Feb._1947_%28William_P._Gottlieb_04251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thu